# Response headers for Cloudflare Pages.
#
# `public/` is copied into `dist/` verbatim, so this file ships as
# `dist/_headers` and Pages parses it rather than serving it. `vite preview`
# does NOT read it — the only place these headers can be observed is a
# deployment, which is why spec 032 proves them on a Pages preview before
# production. A header asserted from local serving is not a verified header.
#
# Comments and blank lines sit at column 0 only. An indented line inside a rule
# block is parsed as a header, so the commentary lives here rather than beside
# the directives it explains.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------- precedence
#
# Cloudflare Pages MERGES every rule whose pattern matches, and joins repeated
# header names with a comma. Quoting the docs: "An incoming request which
# matches multiple rules' URL patterns will inherit all rules' headers", and
# "If a header is applied twice in the _headers file, the values are joined
# with a comma separator."
#
# There is no last-match-wins and no most-specific-wins. A narrower rule that
# simply re-stated `Cache-Control` would be SERVED ALONGSIDE the broad one —
# `public, max-age=31536000, immutable, public, max-age=0, must-revalidate` —
# and which half a given cache honours is not something to find out in
# production. So the two un-hashed files below detach the inherited value with
# `! Cache-Control` before setting their own, which is the documented way to
# "remove ... a header which has been added by a more pervasive rule". The
# detaching rules come after the rule they detach from, as in Cloudflare's own
# example.
#
# This is the one behaviour here that cannot be proven from the repository.
# Verify it live, on the preview, before merging:
#
#   curl -sI https://<preview>/assets/maplibre-gl-worker.mjs | grep -i cache-
#     -> cache-control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate    (exactly this)
#
# `src/headers.test.ts` holds the structure — which rules exist, in which
# order, carrying which directives — so this file cannot drift silently.
#
# ------------------------------------------------------------------- the CSP
#
# Every source is derived from code in this repository, not from a template:
#
#   default-src 'self'   everything unnamed is same-origin.
#   script-src           the hashed bundle, plus ONE inline script: the
#                        pre-paint theme setter in index.html. The hash covers
#                        that script's exact text, so editing it without
#                        recomputing breaks it — visibly but harmlessly, as a
#                        light flash on a dark reload. Recompute with:
#                          python3 -c "import re,hashlib,base64;s=re.search(r'<script(?![^>]*src=)[^>]*>(.*?)</script>',open('index.html').read(),re.S).group(1);print('sha256-'+base64.b64encode(hashlib.sha256(s.encode()).digest()).decode())"
#                        No 'unsafe-eval': MapLibre v6 reaches `eval` only on
#                        its non-module plugin-loading path, which is not used
#                        here (maplibre-gl-worker.mjs takes the module branch).
#   style-src            'unsafe-inline' for two consumers: index.html's boot
#                        skeleton is an inline <style> (hashable in principle),
#                        and the served og-image page carries literal style=""
#                        attributes. React's style PROPS go through CSSOM,
#                        which style-src does not govern, so the SPA itself
#                        would run under a hash + CSP3 'unsafe-hashes'; that
#                        tightening is available if the og-image page ever
#                        gets its own detached CSP. (Comment corrected in
#                        review — the first draft blamed the chart style
#                        props, a false premise a future tightening would
#                        have been argued against.)
#   img-src data:        maplibre-gl.css draws its zoom controls from
#                        `url("data:image/svg+xml…")`.
#   img-src blob:        maplibre-gl-shared.mjs decodes tile and sprite images
#                        through `URL.createObjectURL(blob)`.
#   tiles.openfreemap.org  the basemap, in img-src and connect-src: style JSON,
#                        vector tiles, raster shading, sprites and glyphs all
#                        resolve to that one origin — verified against both the
#                        positron and dark styles StationMap.tsx names.
#   font-src data:       a site-wide LOOSENING whose only consumer is the
#                        served og-image page (its typeface is a data: URI so
#                        the card renders identically wherever screenshotted).
#                        The site's own fonts are same-origin files from
#                        @fontsource-variable and need only 'self'. Kept
#                        because a data: font is marginal risk; the tighter
#                        alternative is a detached per-path CSP for the
#                        og-image page.
#   worker-src blob:     MapLibre spawns its tile-parsing worker from a Blob
#                        that imports /assets/maplibre-gl-worker.mjs; child-src
#                        repeats it for browsers that predate worker-src.
#   frame-ancestors      nothing embeds this site.
#   form-action 'self'   there are no forms; a form submitting anywhere is an
#                        injection, not a feature.

/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=(), payment=()
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; form-action 'self'; script-src 'self' 'sha256-hHg0jcnC383GhRP1+/aWHqYMomwqyngDodKphzQfk+U='; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob: https://tiles.openfreemap.org; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https://tiles.openfreemap.org; worker-src 'self' blob:; child-src blob:; manifest-src 'self'

# Vite content-addresses everything in /assets/ except the two files below, so
# a change to any of them changes its name. A year, immutable.

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# The exceptions, and the reason this file needs the detach syntax at all.
# MapLibre resolves `maplibre-gl-worker.mjs` against `import.meta.url` inside a
# template string at runtime, so Rollup cannot see it and cannot hash it —
# vite.config.ts emits both files verbatim under their literal names. An
# immutable year on an un-hashed file is a year of blank maps after an upgrade.

/assets/maplibre-gl-worker.mjs
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

/assets/maplibre-gl-shared.mjs
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# The social card. Short, not immutable: its name is fixed by index.html's
# `og:image`, so it is re-uploaded under the same path whenever it is redrawn,
# and the crawlers that fetch it do so rarely.

/og-image.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600

# Its source composition ships because `public/` ships whole. It is a build
# input, not a page of this site, and it says so in its own <meta> too.

# Pages' clean URLs serve this page at /og-image (the .html path answers
# 308) — found in review, where the rule was keyed to the redirect and the
# only working noindex was the page's own <meta>. Both paths carry the
# header now; verifiable on production only, because every *.pages.dev
# preview response gets a platform x-robots-tag regardless.
/og-image
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
/og-image.html
  X-Robots-Tag: noindex
